WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.360
A Pacinian fibre typically fires at the press and at the release.

2
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.540
In between, it is silent.

3
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:11.920
Where does that brevity come from?

4
00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:14.053
There are three suspects.

5
00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:16.313
First, the capsule.

6
00:00:17.233 --> 00:00:21.133
Its onion of layers could absorb a held press before it reaches the ending.

7
00:00:22.183 --> 00:00:23.723
Second, the ending's channels.

8
00:00:24.623 --> 00:00:27.823
They could open at the press, then close while the press is still held.

9
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:30.433
Third, the spike generator.

10
00:00:31.373 --> 00:00:34.753
It could stop firing even while the ending stays depolarized.

11
00:00:35.683 --> 00:00:42.143
Two terms. The generator potential is the ending's graded depolarization, driven by

12
00:00:42.143 --> 00:00:43.343
the transduction current.

13
00:00:44.283 --> 00:00:49.403
Impulses are the all-or-none action potentials it triggers further along the axon.

14
00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:52.367
The classic suspect was the capsule.

15
00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:58.627
In 1966, Loewenstein and Skalak modelled it as fluid between elastic layers.

16
00:00:59.717 --> 00:01:04.917
Follow one press. At the instant of the press, the fluid cannot move fast enough.

17
00:01:05.817 --> 00:01:06.817
The ending is squeezed.

18
00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:11.850
During the hold, the fluid flows and the stretched layers take up the load.

19
00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.950
The core relaxes.

20
00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:18.453
At the release, the layers spring back and jolt the core a second time.

21
00:01:19.417 --> 00:01:23.757
So, in this model, the capsule strongly damps steady pressure and passes quick

22
00:01:23.757 --> 00:01:26.217
change. That is a high-pass filter.

23
00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:33.497
A year earlier, in 1965, Loewenstein and Mendelson peeled most layers from cat

24
00:01:33.497 --> 00:01:36.017
corpuscles. Then they pressed and held.

25
00:01:37.217 --> 00:01:41.937
Predict. If the capsule did all the work, what should now last through the hold?

26
00:01:47.967 --> 00:01:53.627
Only half of it. The generator potential decayed much more slowly, mainly under

27
00:01:53.627 --> 00:01:54.627
intense compression.

28
00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.550
But the impulses did not persist.

29
00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.770
The ending typically still fired a single spike.

30
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.460
So brevity had two stages.

31
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.260
One is the mechanics around the ending.

32
00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.120
The other is the spike-generating membrane.

33
00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:17.033
In 2025, researchers recorded at the ending itself.

34
00:02:18.013 --> 00:02:19.693
They used bill skin from duck embryos.

35
00:02:20.867 --> 00:02:24.587
They removed the onion, and kept the inner cells that hug the ending.

36
00:02:25.617 --> 00:02:30.937
Predict. If the onion sets the brief response, what should happen to the ending's

37
00:02:30.937 --> 00:02:31.937
current?

38
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:42.330
It stayed fast. And the fibre's frequency tuning did not change significantly.

39
00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.020
The current did grow larger.

40
00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:48.000
So the onion may still damp the force that arrives.

41
00:02:52.083 --> 00:02:53.663
How do the two results fit?

42
00:02:54.503 --> 00:02:57.743
In the duck, currents slowed only as stripped endings deteriorated.

43
00:02:58.967 --> 00:03:03.087
So a damaged, dying ending can look like one that has lost its filter.

44
00:03:03.927 --> 00:03:04.927
That is one reading.

45
00:03:05.917 --> 00:03:11.397
Keep this. In this duck preparation, the ending stayed fast without the outer core.

46
00:03:12.317 --> 00:03:14.997
So fast adaptation does not need the onion there.
